  "findings": [
    "ParticipantBox#getCenterX/getMaxX uses ComponentRoseParticipant#getPreferredWidth, which includes deltaShadow; painted head rectangles do not. The new living-participant group member includes the resolved shadow extent and simple shadowed group controls pass.",
    "Adding a spanning note makes focused controls fail for both engines. Legacy checker_focus_shadow_span1_e0 gives frame width187.9014 Java versus186.9014 Rust and a1px participant shift. The fresh wide primary note polygon is x22..370 in Java versus23..368 in Rust. over_several_note_geometry and the group note envelope still reconstruct p2.getMaxX from painted box_width, so the planned propagation into multi-participant note allocation is incomplete.",
    "Four of twelve independent participant-shadow cases pass; eight mismatch. The omission is source-traced, not an unexplained tuning residual.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
  ],
